  "prefLabel": "Liq 801.01 Chapter 224:91-Laws of 2011, Liquor Commission",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Liq 801.01 Chapter 224:91-Laws of 2011, Liquor Commission. Employee Incentive Program, provides that the:\n\n(a) The purpose of these rules is to implement an employee incentive system for monetary incentives for its store managers and employees to reward superior customer service, organization, and appearance of retail stores, creativity and attractiveness of displays, workplace safety records, and other relevant and objective criteria related to customer service and sales.\n\nSource. #13469, eff 10-22-22 (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Liq 800)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/liq100-1100.html"
